1. Change admin password to 40+ character random string
2. Enable and test audit logging with immutable table
3. Hash all passwords in users table with bcrypt
4. Encrypt secrets table using pgp_sym_encrypt
5. Remove unnecessary superuser backdoor_admin or change its password
6. Review and potentially remove admin_temp and file_test tables

**Phase 2 (This week):**
7. Implement RLS policies on users/audit tables
8. Enable SSL/TLS connections (hostssl in pg_hba.conf)
9. Add foreign key constraints to audit_log
10. Restrict function creation privileges
11. Review application code for SQL injection vulnerabilities

**Phase 3 (This month):**
12. Implement secrets management solution (HashiCorp Vault / AWS Secrets Manager)
13. Set up connection limits per role
14. Enable comprehensive query logging and log rotation
15. Conduct security code review of application queries
16. Implement schema-level RBAC with principle of least privilege

